{"name":"Pitch","hex":"#423937","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pitch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sticky, gummy substance secreted by trees; tree sap.","Anything similar to or derived from tree sap: resin; rosin."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or smear with pitch.","To darken; to blacken; to obscure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pitch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pitch (music)","blocks":[{"text":"Pitch is the quality that makes it possible to judge sounds as \"higher\" and \"lower\" in the sense associated with musical melodies. Pitch is a perceptual property that allows sounds to be ordered on a frequency-related scale. \nPitch is a major auditory attribute of musical tones, along with duration, loudness, and timbre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Bach_-_Taylor_1873.png/330px-Bach_-_Taylor_1873.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitch_(music)","wikidata":"Q118819"},{"title":"Absolute pitch","blocks":[{"text":"Absolute pitch (AP), often called perfect pitch, is the ability to identify or re-create a given pitch without the benefit of a reference tone. AP may be demonstrated using linguistic labelling, associating mental imagery with the note, or sensorimotor responses. For example, an AP possessor can accurately reproduce a heard tone on a musical instrument without \"hunting\" for the correct pitch. However, pitch labelling is less common than pitch recall."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absolute_pitch","wikidata":"Q213250"},{"title":"Pitch (card game)","blocks":[{"text":"Pitch is an American trick-taking game equivalent to the British blind all fours which, in turn, is derived from the classic all fours. Historically, pitch started as \"blind all fours\", a very simple all fours variant that is still played in England as a pub game. The modern game involving a bidding phase and setting back a party's score if the bid is not reached came up in the middle of the 19th century and is more precisely known as auction pitch or setback."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitch_(card_game)","wikidata":"Q1823090"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/C3_131_Hz_oscillogram.png/120px-C3_131_Hz_oscillogram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/C3_131_Hz_oscillogram.png/250px-C3_131_Hz_oscillogram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/C3_131_Hz_oscillogram.png/120px-C3_131_Hz_oscillogram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AC3_131_Hz_oscillogram.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Middle_C%2C_or_262_hertz%2C_on_a_virtual_oscilloscope.png/120px-Middle_C%2C_or_262_hertz%2C_on_a_virtual_oscilloscope.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Middle_C%2C_or_262_hertz%2C_on_a_virtual_oscilloscope.png/250px-Middle_C%2C_or_262_hertz%2C_on_a_virtual_oscilloscope.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Middle_C%2C_or_262_hertz%2C_on_a_virtual_oscilloscope.png/120px-Middle_C%2C_or_262_hertz%2C_on_a_virtual_oscilloscope.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMiddle_C%2C_or_262_hertz%2C_on_a_virtual_oscilloscope.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/C5_523_Hz_oscillogram.png/120px-C5_523_Hz_oscillogram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/C5_523_Hz_oscillogram.png/250px-C5_523_Hz_oscillogram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/C5_523_Hz_oscillogram.png/120px-C5_523_Hz_oscillogram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AC5_523_Hz_oscillogram.png"}],"sounds":{"pitch":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/En-us-pitch.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/ff/En-us-pitch.ogg/En-us-pitch.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/En-au-pitch.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/80/En-au-pitch.ogg/En-au-pitch.ogg.mp3"}]}}}